{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>From the days of</b> — Rather like <i>מזקנים אתבונן</i> (Psalms 119:100, 'from the elders I discern'), <i>מאויבי תחכמני</i> (Psalms 119:98, 'from my enemies you make me wise'). The meaning: there they stood upon the sins of his generation as if they stood with the children of Benjamin — they are <b>sons of worthlessness</b>, like <i>עולה</i> [worthlessness], and it was <b>for a trembling</b>, and it was only trembling, <b>and today they do not fear</b> that war should overtake them as it overtook the children of Benjamin from the tribes. And this is like <i>כריח שדה</i> (Genesis 27:27), whose sense is: see the smell of my sons whom YHWH blessed — <i>כריח שדה</i> (like the smell of a field)."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The comment quotes three forms from Hosea 10:9 but with variant spellings: עלוה for עלוה (Hosea has בני עלוה), לזעוה / רק זועה for לזעוה (Hosea has ויהיו לזעוה); these are retained as they appear in the Hebrew comment. The forms מזקנים אתבונן and מאויבי תחכמני are quoted with conversive bet/mem prefixes (מן assimilated), as in Ibn Ezra's cited forms."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:53.728374427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}